==Strategy==
This stage is designed to be unfair. With a boss with extreme health, damage, ridiculous range and an unfair Freeze and Weaken that lasts way too long, this stage is going to be quite the piece of work to take down without any EVA Angel Super Rares or Uber Rares. Awakened EVA Unit-13 is also immune to basically everything, meaning that the only viable Cannons you should bring are either the [[Ototo Corps#Iron Wall|Iron Wall]] or [[Ototo Corps#Slow Beam|Slow Beam]] specifically for the peons—this also means that the only way to push EVA Unit-13 back is with the [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] powerup. Additionally, money is seldom supplied in this stage, so bringing a [[Battle Items#Rich Cat|Rich Cat]] is also encouraged.

Regarding stalling EVA Unit-13, because of its ridiculous Omni Strike and CC, bringing meatshields like Metal Cat is not advised whatsoever, and neither is chipping it down with Cyberpunk. In order to stall him, your main tools will most likely be [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] alongside a bunch of Research [[Cat Combo]]s, as well as [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]] who does better to stall the boss if there's Trolly Bloggers, as its damage is enough to kill them mostly consistently.

Aside from EVA Unit-13 itself, its peons are Shibalien, B.B Bunny, and the aforementioned Trolly Blogger. Similar to stages like Floor 30, the peons are initially isolated but start overlapping over time, meaning that the longer you take the harder it becomes to clear each peon wave. For isolated peons, [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] is incredible to get a small cash boost, while [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] has high damage and speed, and can actually attack more than once before it gets one-shot by EVA Unit-13. When peons start clumping together, your best units to clear dense waves will be [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]], who can connect onto every enemy here consistently, [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] who has extreme health and whose Surge can chip down EVA Unit-13, and a Talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], who after killing the peons can get a good two hundred thousand damage onto EVA Unit-13 before dying. During periods of downtime, chip EVA Unit-13 with Manic Lion, Fishman, Bullet Train, and Bahamut, and over the course of a couple of minutes you'll be able to clear each peon wave and kill the boss. Note that while EVA Unit-13 does have Strengthen, it does nothing, at least on {{1c}}, as everything either already dies or lives a hit anyways. On {{2c}}, it now oneshots the Cat Base at any level, removing the opportunity to push it off with Sniper the Cat.

If you do have any [[:Category:EVA Angel Killer Cats|EVA Angel Killers]], simply spam them whilst using [[You Will Find Happiness (Combo)|You Will Find Happiness]], and they should be able to kill the peons and EVA Unit-13 soon after. In this case, bring the Curseblast Cannon to remove EVA Unit-13's annoying Freeze and Weaken.

==='''3 Crown'''===
On 3 Crown, this stage goes from tedious to really, really hard, to the point where there are less than a hundred recorded clears of this stage without EVA Angel Killers. Due to the magnifications being upscaled threefold, on 3 Crown you now need to fight a twelve million health boss who can one-shot Rock and Doron when Strengthened, supported by cosmic horrors like 108,000 health Shibaliens. Doing this stage without EVA Angel Killers is highly discouraged for your own sanity, but if you really want to challenge yourself, see the Walkthrough section for an in-depth guide. Even with EVA Angel Killers, you can't just mindlessly spam Super Rares, as the peons have way too much health, proper timing is necessary alongside the proper usage of ordinary units such as Awakened Bahamut Cat.

Cat Combos will be essential in facilitating certain interactions with specific units. [[Drinking Age (Combo)|Drinking Age]] in particular grants a 10% speed boost that makes the attrition game much more forgiving when it comes to timing your units (so long as you can get used to the new deployment windows and prevent your units' attacks from missing due to mistimed Sniper the Cats). You can pair this up with either [[Spinners (Combo)|Spinners]] for even faster speed, or [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] for better recharge on all of your cats. It is needless to say why this in itself is so invaluable, but the Cat Combo also contains [[Mr. (Special Cat)|Mr.]], who serves as a competent tertiary meatshield. If you own [[Maneki Cat (Special Cat)|Maneki Cat]], you can use [[Thanks for All (Combo)|Thanks for All]] to increase bounties from enemies-especially useful if you find yourself struggling financially.

'''Sniper the Cat can detriment you if used recklessly.''' Assuming Unit-13 is completely held in place, Sniper the Cat will fail to interrupt its attack within a 1-frame margin every three attack cycles. This leads to Unit-13 attacking, getting its backswing animation reset, and attacking again instantly.

The following are most of the relevant peon elemination combinations:

Trolly Blogger
*7 M.Lion hits
*Everything else.
B.B. Bunny
*x2 Slime^ // B.Train // Courier // Fishman^ (Lv.53)
*Supercar
Shibalien
*Supercar + Slime // B.Train // Fishman^
*Supercar + Slime^ + Stone // Courier // Fishman
*Slime + B.Train + Fishman
*Slime + B.Train + Stone + Courier + 2x M.Lion hits
*2x Slime + Stone + Fishman
*2x Slime + Stone + Courier + Stone // Courier
*2x Slime + B.Train // Fishman^
Every unit assumed Lv.50 unless stated otherwise<br>
Slime^ = Weaken Wave damage<br>
Fishman^ = Attack Buff Talents

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]]: Manic Lion is fast and is your primary meatshield across every crown. For 1 crown, a high-level Manic Lion provides good chip damage and defence to the peons but heavily falls off on 2 crowns. For 3 Crown, make sure Manic Lion is above level 40 to allow him to tank a B.B Bunny hit without staggering immediately.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]]: A near indestructible speedy meatshield who stalls Unit-13 and its supporting peons and also kills Trolly Blogger. Note that on 3 Crown, level 50 Stone will get one-shot by EVA Unit-13's Strengthen, and on 2 Crown, Level 36 and below suffers the same fate. Try to reserve Stone as a secondary supporting meatshield to Manic Lion as its cooldown is slightly longer.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: With its True Form, Jelly Dumpling is able to unleash a huge Wave which one-shots B.B Bunny on 1 and 2 Crown. Be careful because even with the +5 speed, it is still extremely difficult for Jelly Dumpling to rush and attack Unit-13 without losing space. Note that if Jelly Dumpling dies to Unit-13, any remaining Wave is Weakened. Avoid these problems by utilizing the Sniper Powerup to interrupt Unit-13's attack while Slime rushes in and lands a full attack and Wave before dying.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Massive vs. Red makes Courier the best tool to deal with B.B Bunny. Long-Distance is a double edged sword here: the extended reach helps hit peons behind the enemy frontline, easily noticeable with Trolly Blogger, but the blindspot forces a meatshield to be used when interacting with B.B. Bunny.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train]]: Bullet Train performs well on every crown difficulty. It has an excellent damage output (47,250 at Lv.50) with a very fast speed, meaning you can quickly clear a path to the boss while chipping peons substantially. Apply its Double Bounty on the B.B. Bunny (on 3 crown it will not 1-shot) if you run out of cash.
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]]: A quick, expendable source of burst damage that can be used in a pinch to clear out small peons. Varying +levels can change certain interactions, so conduct some research to fully understand what unit combinations can achieve what.
*[[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]]: Aim to deliver Supercar's 81,000 damage to Shibaliens (to eliminate) or Unit-13 (for chip). Keep in mind that Supercar needs a meatshield to be hit first to then land its hit on Shibalien, B.B.Bunny has no such requirements. Supercar has a similar recharge to Bullet Train, so a handy tip is to only deploy one when the other is around halfway recharged to be less vulnerable to the next peon wave.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: With Talents, Bahamut's Explosion now doubles his effective damage and also removes dense waves of peons even on 3 Crown. For maximum efficiency, combine him with a Sniper-interrupt to gain an additional hit. Even with a 2.5 minute cooldown, his sheer power significantly reduces stage playtime and provides a clear win condition of repeatedly cycling Bahamut until victory. If you want to further maximize his performance, equip a Dodge Attack Ability Orb on him for the potential to occasionally survive a Unit-13 attack and wreak more havoc.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]]: A disposable nuker that easily clears a dense wave of peons approximately every 1 minute. Ideally use Doron's True Form as it has higher speed. On 2 crown, Level 33+ Doron in any form survives strengthened Unit-13's attack. Similar to Stone, Doron gets one-shot on 3 Crown if Unit-13 is strengthened, so plan to use it with a Sniper Interrupt.
*[[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Master of Mind Soractes]]: On 2 and 3 crowns, Soractes is beneficial: not for the unit but instead for the Conjure Spirit. He recharges every 2 minutes and is expensive, so spare him to clear out a tough wave with 2 Shibaliens. For 1 crown, it is better to spend your funds in deploying more Manic Lions, Stones and Couriers - with or without a Research Combo - since the peons are just too weak to justify Soractes.
*[[Superfeline (Normal Cat)|True Superfeline]]: Superfeline has good Omni Strike burst, 41 speed and cooldown like Bullet Train. It does great by itself on 1 and 2 crown, and on 3 crown pair it with Courier to quickly clear out a Shibalien wave. Since it is very expensive to deploy, Superfeline should be only be used in an emergency, and at a pinch at that because of his exorbitant price tag.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
''The only Ubers that could even stand a chance here due to EVA Unit-13's unfair design are EVA Angel Killers. Even with them, many will not make the stage a free clear, especially on {{3c}} due to their lack of immunities to EVA Unit-13's crowd-control abilitities.''
*[[One-Eyed Asuka (Uber Rare Cat)|One-Eyed Asuka]]: Among the EVA Angel Killer Ubers, Asuka is by far the best in this stage. With her Freeze Immunity, Asuka tears through this stage with her sheer damage. Asuka's Surge is also great here, being able to damage EVA Unit-13 even more as well as either killing or severely damaging the peons.

